    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "I'll start by reading the entry point."
    },
    {
     "type": "tool_use",
     "id": "toolu_01",
     "name": "Read",
     "input": {
      "file_path": "{PROJECT}/src/main.rs"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Now I'll generate the build log."
    },
    {
     "type": "tool_use",
     "id": "toolu_02",
     "name": "Bash",
     "input": {
      "command": "touch build.log && seq 1 40",
      "description": "Generate the build log"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "tool_use",
     "id": "toolu_03",
     "name": "Edit",
     "input": {
      "file_path": "{PROJECT}/src/main.rs",
      "old_string": "println!(\"hello\");",
      "new_string": "println!(\"hello, world\");"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "tool_use",
     "id": "toolu_04",
     "name": "Bash",
     "input": {
      "command": "cat missing.txt",
      "description": "Show the missing file"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "## Summary\n\nThe project is a **tiny Rust binary** with one entry point:\n\n- `src/main.rs` prints a greeting\n- `README.md` describes the project\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. Updated the greeting to `hello, world`\n2. Generated `build.log`\n\n```rust\nfn main() {\n    println!(\"hello, world\");\n}\n```\n\n| File | Status |\n|------|--------|\n| src/main.rs | modified |\n| build.log | created |\n\n> Note: `missing.txt` does not exist, so that step failed."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "steps": [
  {
